@SOURCE@ (580.196.07-1+sparky2+lc1) unstable; urgency=medium, binary-only=yes

  * NVIDIA's package 580.196.07-1 from NVIDIA's CUDA repository for Debian
    12, carried by Sparky Stereo OS for Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards
    (ORDER 354): NVIDIA publishes its 580 driver for Debian only there, and
    Debian 14's APT refuses that repository's key (a SHA-1 binding
    signature). NVIDIA's files and maintainer scripts are unchanged, byte
    for byte, with their modes: the NVIDIA Software License distributes the
    binary files only unmodified (1.1(d)(i), 2.3).
  * The control file is the edition's: the version, NVIDIA's exact
    relations among the carried packages at this version (with
    nvidia-kernel-dkms, which the edition's nvidia-legacy-580xx-kernel-dkms
    provides at it), the maintainer (NVIDIA stays as Original-Maintainer),
    the homepage, the bug tracker and a note in the description; where
    NVIDIA's package ships ELF files and declares no dependency at all
    (libnvidia-nscq), the dependency dpkg-shlibdeps derives from them.
  * nvidia-kernel-support does not Provide, Conflict with or Replace
    nvidia-detect, as NVIDIA's package does (NVIDIA's own nvidia-detect is
    an empty transitional package). On Debian nvidia-detect is the real
    detector, Hardware Setup runs /usr/bin/nvidia-detect, the two packages
    share no file, and with the Provides apt 3.3's dist-upgrade replaced
    Debian's nvidia-detect with nvidia-kernel-support (ORDER 390). Its other
    Provides, Conflicts and Replaces are NVIDIA's.
  * Added: README.sparky-stereo, this entry and the Lean Code manifest,
    which records every NVIDIA file as kept as NVIDIA ships it; and, in the
    packages NVIDIA ships without one (its i386 packages, cuda-drivers),
    NVIDIA's copyright file, byte for byte the one its amd64 packages ship
    (NVIDIA Software License 1.1(d)(ii); Debian Policy 2.3).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0300
